PYTHON-SPECIFIC ATTACK VECTORS TO HUNT (/python/packages/**)
━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

  [PY-1] DANGEROUS EXECUTION PRIMITIVES
    - eval(), exec(), compile(), subprocess with shell=True, os.system()
    - Hunt: is any of this reachable with LLM-generated or tool-call args?

  [PY-2] UNSAFE DESERIALIZATION
    - pickle.load/loads, yaml.load (without SafeLoader), marshal
    - Hunt: is any deserialized data attacker/network/tool-output controlled?

  [PY-3] PATH TRAVERSAL / ARBITRARY FILE ACCESS
    - open(), os.path.join(), shutil operations using LLM-supplied paths
    - Hunt: file-read/file-write/upload tools — can "../" or absolute paths
      escape an intended sandbox directory?

  [PY-4] SSRF IN HTTP / FETCH TOOLS
    - requests/httpx/aiohttp calls where the URL/host comes from LLM output
    - Hunt: is there validation against internal IPs, localhost, cloud
      metadata endpoints (169.254.169.254), or scheme allowlisting?
    - Hunt specifically: if a "safe" fetch tool is disabled/denied, does the
      agent fall back to a raw shell/curl/requests call instead? (This exact
      pattern is a known real-world bug class in agentic IDE tools.)

  [PY-5] ASYNC RACE CONDITIONS / SHARED STATE
    - asyncio tasks sharing mutable state (agent memory, session state)
    - Hunt: TOCTOU between permission checks and tool execution

  [PY-6] SILENT ERROR SWALLOWING
    - bare except:, except Exception: pass, .get() masking failures
    - Critical if it hides a failed auth/permission/validation check

  [PY-7] TYPE CONFUSION ON TOOL-CALL ARGUMENTS
    - LLM function-calling arguments arrive as untyped JSON/dict — is there
      real schema validation before use, or trust-on-parse?

  [PY-8] DEPENDENCY VULNERABILITIES
    - Check pyproject.toml / requirements for outdated/vulnerable packages

