  [NET-2] REFLECTION-BASED DYNAMIC DISPATCH
    - Activator.CreateInstance / Type.GetType / MethodInfo.Invoke driven by
      LLM-supplied tool/type/method names — can arbitrary types be invoked?

  [NET-3] PROCESS / SHELL EXECUTION
    - Process.Start with unsanitized arguments from tool calls

  [NET-4] PATH TRAVERSAL
    - Path.Combine with attacker-controlled segments (does not stop
      absolute-path or ".." escapes)

  [NET-5] SSRF IN HttpClient USAGE
    - Same as PY-4: URL/host validation, internal network protection,
      fallback-to-shell behavior when a controlled tool is blocked

  [NET-6] XXE / UNSAFE XML PARSING
    - XmlDocument/XmlReader without DTD processing disabled

  [NET-7] CONCURRENCY BUGS
    - shared state across async Tasks, missing locks, deadlocks

  [NET-8] DEPENDENCY VULNERABILITIES
    - outdated/vulnerable NuGet packages

